## 1. Brand, voice and tone

**B-1.** Brand name is **2VP**. Legal name **2VP Construction**. Never abbreviate further (no "2V", no "VP").

**B-2.** Voice is **plain-English, confident, technical when it matters**. We write the way a senior project manager talks to a serious homeowner: short sentences, named trades, no jargon for jargon's sake, no marketing fluff. If a sentence could appear on any builder's site, rewrite it until it can only appear on ours.

**B-3.** Never use phrases like "passionate about", "your dream home", "we love what we do". They are conversion-neutral and brand-negative.

**B-4.** UK English everywhere (`-ise`, `-our`, `colour`, `behaviour`, `programme` not `program`). British currency formatting (`£250,000` or `£250k`, never `$` or commas-as-decimals).

**B-5.** Phone: `020 8050 8968`. Email: `hi@2vp.uk`. These appear identically on every page (header, footer, CTAs). NAP consistency is non-negotiable — also required on Google Business Profile.

**B-6.** Primary colour `#0a3d62` (brand), accent `#e6a23c` (brand.accent). Ink `#0b1220`. Don't introduce new brand colours without updating `tailwind.config.ts` and this document.

---

## 2. Service catalogue

**S-1.** Four canonical services. Listed in this order on every page that mentions multiple services:

1. **House Extensions** — single and double-storey rear, side-return, wrap-around.
2. **Loft Conversions** — dormer, mansard, hip-to-gable, L-shape, Velux.
3. **Full Refurbishments** — whole-house strip-out, structural, M&E, joinery, decoration.
4. **Kitchens & Bathrooms** — bespoke installs, en-suites, wet rooms, stone, tiling.

**S-2.** No additional services may be added to the site without updating `src/data/services.ts`, this section, and the rules in §11.

**S-3.** Each service ALWAYS appears with the same four bullets defined in `src/data/services.ts`. Variations across area pages are not allowed.

---

## 3. Geographic coverage (59 areas)

**G-1.** The site explicitly targets **all 33 London boroughs + 26 prime / high-intent areas = 59 area pages**. The canonical list lives in `src/data/areas.ts`.

**G-2.** No area page may be added without:
- a unique slug
- a real postcode list
- a 1-2 sentence "character" paragraph
- a 1-2 sentence "planning" paragraph
- 3-5 neighbouring slugs for internal linking

**G-3.** No area page may be removed without a 301 redirect (in `next.config.mjs`) pointing to the most semantically similar surviving area.

**G-4.** Boroughs and prime areas are tagged via `type: "borough" | "prime"`. Prime areas may live inside a borough's territory (e.g. Mayfair inside Westminster). This duplication is intentional — we want both queries to land on the most relevant page.

**G-5.** Pricing tier (`prime` / `inner` / `outer`) is set in `src/lib/pricing.ts`. Adding a new area requires explicitly assigning it to a tier in `PRIME_SLUGS` or `INNER_SLUGS`, otherwise it defaults to `outer`.

### Master area list (frozen)

**33 boroughs:** City of London, Barking and Dagenham, Barnet, Bexley, Brent, Bromley, Camden, Croydon, Ealing, Enfield, Greenwich, Hackney, Hammersmith and Fulham, Haringey, Harrow, Havering, Hillingdon, Hounslow, Islington, Kensington and Chelsea, Kingston upon Thames, Lambeth, Lewisham, Merton, Newham, Redbridge, Richmond upon Thames, Southwark, Sutton, Tower Hamlets, Waltham Forest, Wandsworth, Westminster.

**26 prime / high-intent:** Mayfair, Notting Hill, Chelsea, Knightsbridge, Belgravia, Marylebone, Fitzrovia, Soho, Kensington, Holland Park, Hampstead, Highgate, Primrose Hill, St John's Wood, Shoreditch, Clapham, Battersea, Fulham, Wimbledon, Putney, Dulwich, Blackheath, Angel, Stoke Newington, Wapping, Canary Wharf.

