## 4. Pricing model

**P-1.** Three tiers map every area to per-square-metre price bands:

| Tier   | Extensions    | Lofts         | Refurbishments | Kitchens & Bathrooms |
|--------|---------------|---------------|----------------|----------------------|
| Prime  | £4,200–6,500  | £2,800–4,200  | £2,600–4,200   | £2,200–4,000         |
| Inner  | £3,200–4,800  | £2,200–3,400  | £2,000–3,200   | £1,800–3,200         |
| Outer  | £2,600–3,800  | £1,800–2,800  | £1,500–2,400   | £1,400–2,600         |

**P-2.** These bands are **indicative only** and must always be qualified with "indicative" or "typical" copy on the page (already in `PriceBands.tsx`).

**P-3.** Final per-project quotes come from the calculator on `2vp.uk/calculator`. Marketing pages must never display a fixed price for a specific job.

**P-4.** Pricing tier labels shown to users use **neutral language**: "London suburban", "inner London", "prime central London". Never write "outer-tier" in user-facing copy (it reads as a downgrade). Internal tier slugs (`prime` / `inner` / `outer`) are for code and analytics only.

**P-5.** When pricing on a real project diverges from the published band by more than ±20% in either direction, the band needs reviewing. Track this in the leads sheet by adding a "Final quote" column.

