## 6. SEO rules — technical

**SEO-T-1.** `metadataBase` is set in `src/app/layout.tsx`. Always source `site.url` from `process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` once preview deploys are in play — never hard-code per deploy.

**SEO-T-2.** Every page must have:
- a unique `<title>` (50–60 chars)
- a unique `<meta name="description">` (140–155 chars)
- a self-referencing `<link rel="canonical">`
- valid Open Graph tags (`og:title`, `og:description`, `og:url`, `og:image`, `og:type`)
- valid Twitter card tags
- one `<h1>` (and exactly one)
- a logical H2/H3 hierarchy

**SEO-T-3.** **NEVER allow the title template to double the brand suffix.** If `generateMetadata` returns a title that already ends in `| 2VP`, the layout template MUST be set to `%s` (not `%s | 2VP`), or the per-page title MUST drop the suffix. Audit on every PR that touches metadata.

**SEO-T-4.** `og:image` is required on every page. Default fallback: `/og-default.jpg` (1200×630, brand-coloured, with the 2VP wordmark). Area pages must additionally generate a per-area image via `src/app/areas/[slug]/opengraph-image.tsx` so previews carry the area name.

**SEO-T-5.** `sitemap.xml` is generated from `src/data/areas.ts`. Any new page type added to the app must also be added to `src/app/sitemap.ts`.

**SEO-T-6.** `robots.txt` allows all crawlers everywhere. Disallow only `/api/`. Re-submit the sitemap in Google Search Console + Bing Webmaster Tools on every meaningful sitemap change.

**SEO-T-7.** Use 301 redirects for any URL change. Never delete a page that has been indexed or linked externally — redirect it.

**SEO-T-8.** Page load: First Contentful Paint < 1.5s on Vercel from London. Largest Contentful Paint < 2.0s. Cumulative Layout Shift < 0.05. Test monthly with Lighthouse + PageSpeed Insights.

**SEO-T-9.** Vercel region is pinned to `lhr1` (London) in `vercel.json`. Don't change without an explicit reason.

---

## 7. SEO rules — on-page

**SEO-O-1.** Title formula for area pages: `Builders in {Area} | Extensions, Lofts & Refurbishments | 2VP`. Never double the `| 2VP`.

**SEO-O-2.** Title formula for service hubs (when built): `{Service} in London | 2VP Construction`.

**SEO-O-3.** Meta description must include: service name, area or "London", a benefit phrase (free calculator / fixed price / one-stop), and never exceed 155 characters.

**SEO-O-4.** H1 must contain the **area name AND at least one service term**. Example: "Extensions, loft conversions & refurbishments in Camden".

**SEO-O-5.** First 100 words of the body must contain the area name at least twice and at least three of the service names.

**SEO-O-6.** Area name density across the page: 0.8% – 1.6%. (Roughly 8–16 mentions in a 1000-word page.) Do not exceed.

**SEO-O-7.** Postcode list is rendered in the hero subhead and in the FAQ ("Do you cover the whole of {area}?"). This is mandatory — postcode queries are high-intent.

**SEO-O-8.** External links to the calculator and booking flow are `dofollow` (we want them to pass authority to 2vp.uk's conversion pages). External links to non-2VP domains (Google reviews, accreditation bodies, planning portals) are `rel="noopener"` and may be `dofollow` only if the destination is a non-competing authority.

---

## 8. SEO rules — schema / JSON-LD

**SEO-S-1.** Every area page emits **four** JSON-LD blocks:

1. `GeneralContractor` (the LocalBusiness sub-type for the area) with `@id` of `${url}#business`. Fields: `name`, `url`, `telephone`, `email`, `image`, `priceRange`, `areaServed`, `address`, `serviceType`.
2. `BreadcrumbList`: Home → Areas → {Area}.
3. `FAQPage`: 5 questions from `buildAreaFAQ()`.
4. `@graph` of 4 `Service` entities — one per service — each with an `Offer` containing `UnitPriceSpecification` (`minPrice`, `maxPrice`, `priceCurrency: GBP`, `unitCode: MTK`, `unitText: "square metre"`).

**SEO-S-2.** The `Service.provider` field MUST reference the LocalBusiness by `@id` (not duplicate the business node). This avoids Google de-duplication issues.

**SEO-S-3.** Validate all schema using <https://search.google.com/test/rich-results> before any change ships to production.

**SEO-S-4.** Once the Google Business Profile is live, add `sameAs` to the LocalBusiness schema pointing at the GBP URL, plus social profiles when those exist.

**SEO-S-5.** When the brand earns reviews on Google or Trustpilot, surface them via `AggregateRating` inside the LocalBusiness node. Never fabricate ratings.

---

## 9. SEO rules — internal linking

**SEO-L-1.** Every area page must link to: 3-5 neighbouring area pages (already wired through `getNeighbours()`), all 4 service hubs (when built), the homepage, the calculator and the booking flow.

**SEO-L-2.** The footer lists ALL 59 area pages on every page of the site. Do not remove or paginate this — it is the primary internal-link graph.

**SEO-L-3.** When the blog (`/insights`) is live, every post must link to at least 2 area pages and 1 service hub, by name, in the body.

**SEO-L-4.** Anchor text variety: avoid using identical anchor for every internal link. Mix natural-language anchors ("our Camden loft conversions", "Hampstead extensions", "see Hackney") rather than just "{Area}" everywhere.

**SEO-L-5.** No orphan pages. Every URL in the sitemap must be reachable from at least one other URL in the sitemap via a `<a href>`.

---

## 10. Keyword rules and target matrix

### 10.1 Head terms (primary)

These are the volume queries every page implicitly targets via H1 + meta:

- `house extensions London`
- `side return extension London`
- `loft conversion London`
- `mansard loft London`
- `house renovation London`
- `house refurbishment London`
- `kitchen fitters London`
- `bathroom installation London`

**K-1.** Head terms are reserved for the **service hub** pages (when built). Area pages should not try to outrank service hubs on bare head terms — they target the head-term × area-modifier intersection.

### 10.2 Area-modifier patterns (the matrix)

For every area `{A}` and every service `{S}`, the following query patterns are in-scope:

- `builders in {A}`
- `construction company {A}`
- `{A} builders`
- `{S} {A}`
- `{S} in {A}`
- `best {S} {A}`
- `how much does a {S} cost in {A}`
- `{S} cost {A}`
- `{S} planning permission {A}`

**K-2.** The H1 covers `builders in {A}` and `{S} in {A}` simultaneously. The price-band block covers cost queries. The FAQ covers planning-permission queries. Do not remove any of these page sections — each one earns a different SERP feature.

### 10.3 Long-tail / informational queries

These are content opportunities for the blog (`/insights`):

- `Article 4 direction {area}`
- `conservation area planning {area}`
- `{area} basement extension policy`
- `party wall agreement London`
- `permitted development rules 2026 London`
- `CIL charges {borough}`
- `mansard vs dormer loft conversion`
- `side return extension steel design`

**K-3.** Every blog post targets exactly one long-tail head intent and links into 2+ area pages by name.

### 10.4 Negative / do-not-target

Avoid targeting these queries — they're noise, low intent, or bad fits:

- Anything mentioning "DIY" — wrong audience
- "Cheap builders London" — wrong positioning
- Locations outside Greater London — dilutes local relevance
- Pure cost queries with no commercial context ("how much is concrete per m³") — informational, not buyer
- "Builder near me" without geographic context — we can't optimise for proximity queries from non-buyers
- "Building regulations London PDF" — not a buyer query, just a downloader

### 10.5 Keyword targeting per page type

| Page type           | Primary intent          | Example primary query                | Example secondary queries                                  |
|---------------------|-------------------------|--------------------------------------|------------------------------------------------------------|
| Home                | Brand + service breadth | `2VP construction London`            | `London builders`, `London construction company`           |
| `/areas/{A}`        | Local intent            | `builders in Camden`                 | `extensions Camden`, `loft conversion NW1`                 |
| `/services/{S}`     | Service head term       | `loft conversions London`            | `mansard loft conversion`, `dormer loft London`            |
| `/insights/{post}`  | Informational long-tail | `Article 4 direction Camden`         | `Camden planning permission`, `Camden conservation area`   |

**K-4.** Cannibalisation rule: two pages on 2vp.uk must not target the same primary query. If a new page would do this, split the intent or merge the pages.

