## 11. Content rules — uniqueness, length, structure

**C-1.** Word count targets:
- Home: 400–600
- Service hub: 1000–1400
- Area page: 600–800 (currently ~750 ✅)
- Blog post: 1200–2000

**C-2.** **Uniqueness floor: no more than 35% of sentences on any area page may be shared with another area page.** Current measured overlap (Camden vs Barnet) is 43% — must be reduced before traffic scales.

**C-3.** Per-area unique blocks (mandatory once content is mature):
- Unique 1-2 sentence `character` paragraph (already in `areas.ts` ✅)
- Unique 1-2 sentence `planning` paragraph (already in `areas.ts` ✅)
- Unique 100–150 word "recent work in {area}" block (TO ADD)
- Unique testimonial OR varied wording on at least 2 of 5 FAQ answers (TO ADD)

**C-4.** Real or representative project mentions must use postcodes (not full addresses) and never name a customer without written consent. Add a "Project consent" column to the leads sheet for tracking.

**C-5.** Stock copy of phrases that appear on every page (Why-2VP grid, Services bullets, contact strip) is allowed as long as the unique copy floor (C-2) is met.

**C-6.** All copy must be original, written for 2VP. No AI-generated content may ship without a human pass that rewrites every paragraph for 2VP voice (see §1).

**C-7.** Spelling / grammar pass required before publishing any new page. UK English (see B-4).

---

## 12. Conversion rules — CTAs, forms, pricing display

**CV-1.** Every area page must show the dual CTA (Calculator + Book Survey) at minimum **three** times: hero, mid-page banner, final block. Already enforced by the template.

**CV-2.** Calculator URL must include `?area={slug}&tier={prime|inner|outer}&postcode={first-postcode}` so the calculator can pre-fill location and apply the tier. Implemented in `buildCalculatorUrl()`.

**CV-3.** Booking URL must include `?area={slug}` so 2VP attribution knows which page produced the survey request.

**CV-4.** Phone number `020 8050 8968` must be visible above the fold on every page (header bar) and clickable as `tel:+442080508968`.

**CV-5.** Lead form rules:
- Required fields: name, email, **project type**, budget, area
- Phone field is **optional** (current page-state has it required — this is on the roadmap to fix; see audit P1 item #9)
- Honeypot field `company` is mandatory and visually hidden via `position: absolute; left: -9999px`
- 1.5 second render gate against bot submissions
- Success state must thank the user, mention the SLA ("within one working day") and provide the phone number for impatient callers

**CV-6.** Pricing display rules:
- Price bands shown on every area page in the order: Extensions → Lofts → Refurbishments → Kitchens & Bathrooms
- Always paired with the disclaimer "indicative ranges only"
- The "Tune my estimate" CTA inside the price-band block deep-links to the calculator with the tuned URL
- Never show a single point price — always a range

**CV-7.** Trust signals (target state, not all yet in place):
- FMB, TrustMark, CHAS, Constructionline, Which? Trusted Trader badges in footer
- Google reviews rating + count strip in hero
- "Featured in" press logos when earned
- Insurance + ICO registration numbers in footer

**CV-8.** Project gallery: every area page should show 3–6 representative project thumbnails. Photography must be real or licensed (no AI-generated imagery without disclosure).

**CV-9.** Urgency / availability indicator: a soft "Booking surveys 2 weeks ahead in {area}" banner near the form is permitted IF the number is true. Never fake urgency.

---

## 13. Tracking and measurement rules

**T-1.** **Tracking is mandatory on every page that ships to production.** A page without analytics may not go live.

**T-2.** Primary analytics: **Vercel Web Analytics** (cookie-less, free, accurate) + **Plausible** (event-level visibility, no consent banner needed). GA4 is acceptable as a parallel if needed for ads attribution; if installed it MUST run under Google Consent Mode v2.

**T-3.** Events to track (snake_case naming):

| Event              | Trigger                                    | Properties                              |
|--------------------|--------------------------------------------|-----------------------------------------|
| `page_view`        | every page load                            | `path`, `area_slug?`, `tier?`           |
| `calculator_click` | any calculator CTA click                   | `area_slug`, `tier`, `placement`        |
| `book_click`       | any booking CTA click                      | `area_slug`, `placement`                |
| `form_start`       | first focus inside the lead form           | `area_slug`                             |
| `form_submit`      | server confirms 200 from `/api/lead`       | `area_slug`, `tier`, `project_type`, `budget` |
| `phone_click`      | `tel:` link click                          | `placement`                             |
| `email_click`      | `mailto:` link click                       | `placement`                             |

**T-4.** Source attribution: pass-through any `utm_*` query params from the landing page into the calculator URL, the booking URL and the `/api/lead` payload. Never strip them.

**T-5.** No tracking pixels for ad platforms (Meta, TikTok, LinkedIn) may be added without an updated cookie banner + consent flow.

**T-6.** Weekly review: every Monday, pull a "previous-7-days" view of `form_submit` count by `area_slug` and `tier`. Use this to prioritise the next week's content / spend.

---

## 14. Lead-handling rules

**L-1.** Leads land in:
1. Google Sheet (via Apps Script web app)
2. `hi@2vp.uk` inbox (internal alert email)
3. The lead's own inbox (confirmation email)

**L-2.** Response SLA: **one working day** maximum from form submission to first human contact. The confirmation email promises this — breaking the promise breaks trust.

**L-3.** Sheet hygiene: every Friday, archive leads older than 90 days that have been converted, lost or marked spam. Keep an audit trail (a second tab) before deleting.

**L-4.** Project-manager assignment: each lead should be assigned to a PM via a "Owner" column in the sheet within 4 working hours of arrival.

**L-5.** Lead status taxonomy in the sheet:
- `new` (default on row append)
- `contacted` (PM called or emailed)
- `survey-booked` (calendar slot held)
- `quoted` (proposal sent)
- `won` (project signed)
- `lost-price`, `lost-timing`, `lost-fit`, `lost-other`
- `spam`

**L-6.** No lead's contact details may be shared outside 2VP without their written consent. Section 17 (legal) governs this.

---

## 15. Email rules

**E-1.** All transactional email (lead alerts + confirmations) is sent from the Apps Script attached to the leads sheet. The script is owned by `hi@2vp.uk` (or "send mail as" is configured), so the From address is `hi@2vp.uk`.

**E-2.** Internal alert email rules:
- Subject: `New 2VP lead — {Name}, {Area} ({Project type})`
- Body includes all lead details
- Reply-To set to the lead's email so hitting Reply contacts the customer directly

**E-3.** Confirmation email rules:
- Subject: `Thanks for getting in touch with 2VP — your {Area} project`
- Plain text (HTML version is a follow-up enhancement)
- Reply-To set to `hi@2vp.uk`
- Always include the calculator URL tuned for the area, the phone number, and an enquiry summary
- Must include an unsubscribe path or be classified strictly as transactional (PECR/CAN-SPAM safe). Currently transactional only — do not repurpose for marketing.

**E-4.** Marketing / nurture emails are out of scope for the current setup. To start nurture sequences, the form needs an explicit "opt-in to receive updates" checkbox and a separate ESP (Resend / SendGrid).

**E-5.** Apps Script daily mail quota: 100/day on free Gmail, 1500/day on Workspace. If volume exceeds 50 leads/day on free or 700/day on Workspace, migrate to a dedicated transactional ESP.

---

## 16. Legal, GDPR and compliance rules

**LG-1.** UK GDPR / Data Protection Act 2018 applies. 2VP is the data controller. ICO registration is mandatory (~£40/year) — confirm it's in place.

**LG-2.** Required pages: `/privacy` and `/terms`. Both must be linked from:
- The footer
- The lead form (under the submit button)
- The cookie banner (when one ships)

**LG-3.** Privacy policy must state:
- What data is collected (name, email, phone, postcode, IP, UA, source URL, project type, budget, message)
- Why (to respond to the enquiry)
- Legal basis (legitimate interest / contract preparation)
- How long retained (90 days after last contact unless converted)
- Who has access (2VP staff + Google as Sheets host)
- Data subject rights and the contact route to exercise them
- DPO / privacy contact email (`privacy@2vp.uk` recommended)

**LG-4.** Cookie banner: required only if non-essential cookies / tracking pixels are added. Vercel Web Analytics + Plausible do not require one. The moment Meta / TikTok / GA4 (with cookies) lands, the banner must go live and consent must be checked before any non-essential tag fires.

**LG-5.** Form consent copy (current and acceptable): "By submitting you agree to be contacted about your project. We don't share your details." When marketing opt-in is added, it must be a SEPARATE unticked checkbox with explicit copy ("Yes, send me 2VP updates by email").

**LG-6.** Any reviews quoted on the site must use real, attributable names (first name + initial + area is acceptable) and may not be fabricated. Each must be backed by a written or digital record of the customer's permission to publish.

**LG-7.** Construction-specific compliance — keep in mind for content claims:
- CDM 2015 duties — only claim if compliant
- Party Wall etc. Act 1996 — only claim if you handle these in-house
- Building Regulations — only claim if you submit on the client's behalf
- Public liability + employer's liability insurance — only state the cover level you actually carry. Inaccurate claims here are illegal.

---

## 17. Performance, accessibility and security rules

**X-1.** Lighthouse score floor on `/areas/[any]`: 95+ Performance, 95+ SEO, 95+ Best Practices, 95+ Accessibility. Test monthly.

**X-2.** No client-side JavaScript may be added to area pages beyond what the LeadForm already ships. New interactive features must be evaluated for SSR-ability first.

**X-3.** Accessibility:
- WCAG 2.2 AA conformance
- Every form input has a programmatic `<label>` (already in place)
- Body text colour contrast ≥ 4.5:1 against background. Switch any `text-slate-500` body text to `text-slate-600`
- Focus states visible on every interactive element
- All images have `alt` text — descriptive for content images, empty `alt=""` for decorative

**X-4.** Images:
- Use `next/image` (or `<img>` with width/height) — never an unsized `<img>` (CLS hit)
- WebP / AVIF preferred, JPEG fallback
- Lazy-load anything below the fold

**X-5.** Security headers (set in `next.config.mjs` → `headers()`):
- `Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains; preload`
- `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff`
- `Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin`
- `Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()`
- A starter CSP that allows self + Vercel Analytics + Plausible + Google Fonts (once Fonts are introduced)

**X-6.** No third-party scripts may load on form pages without an explicit CSP allowance.

---

## 18. Code, deploy and operational rules

**OP-1.** Branch model: feature branches off `main`. Today's working branch is `claude/london-landing-pages-bOcqW`. After review, merge to `main` and let Vercel auto-deploy.

**OP-2.** Pull-request gate: every PR must pass `npm run build` locally before review. Once CI lands, lint + typecheck become CI-gated too.

**OP-3.** Vercel environment variables:

| Var                          | Where             | Purpose                                    |
|------------------------------|-------------------|--------------------------------------------|
| `LEAD_WEBHOOK_URL`           | production preview | Apps Script web app URL                    |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL`       | production         | `https://2vp.uk` (canonical origin)        |
| `NEXT_PUBLIC_PLAUSIBLE_DOMAIN` | production        | `2vp.uk` (set when Plausible is wired)     |

**OP-4.** Apps Script edits require a new deployment version: **Deploy → Manage deployments → pencil → Version: New version → Deploy**. The web-app URL is stable; Vercel env doesn't change.

**OP-5.** Domain pointing: `2vp.uk` (or `areas.2vp.uk`) is pointed at the Vercel project under **Project → Settings → Domains**.

**OP-6.** Backups: the leads sheet is the system of record while volume is low. Apps Script writes are atomic; Google Drive retains version history. When volume grows, mirror leads to a backed-up CRM.

**OP-7.** Monitoring: Vercel deployment status + Plausible "live visitors" check daily. Set up a Vercel deployment alert email to `hi@2vp.uk`.

**OP-8.** Incident process: if `/api/lead` returns 5xx, leads are dropped. Set up a synthetic POST every 15 minutes via a Vercel cron or external monitor (BetterStack / Checkly). Alert on consecutive failures.

---

## 19. 90-day roadmap (consolidated)

| Week | Theme              | Deliverables |
|------|--------------------|--------------|
| 1    | P0 fixes + tracking | Title double-suffix bug; OG image + per-area generator; install Vercel Analytics + Plausible; `lead_submit`, `calculator_click`, `book_click` events; privacy + terms drafted; security headers in `next.config.mjs`. |
| 2    | Trust assets        | `<ProjectGallery />` component; 6–10 photo assets in `public/projects/`; FMB / TrustMark application started; 3 real testimonials drafted; Google Business Profile created and verified. |
| 3    | Service hubs        | `/services/extensions`, `/services/loft-conversions`, `/services/refurbishments`, `/services/kitchens-bathrooms`. Internal links from every area page. Sitemap + Search Console resubmit. |
| 4    | Friction reduction  | Make phone optional; soft availability banner per area; exit-intent PDF lead magnet ("2VP planning checklist"). |
| 5–6  | Content uniqueness  | Per-area "recent local work" block on 10 areas/week; vary 2 of 5 FAQ answers per area; ensure cross-page sentence overlap < 35%. |
| 7–8  | Insights / blog     | Publish 4 cornerstone pieces: Article 4 directions in Camden; conservation areas in Westminster; loft conversions in Hampstead; RBKC basement policy CL7. |
| 9–10 | PPC variants        | 4–6 narrow LP variants for Google Ads, single-CTA, no nav. Conversion goal wired to GA4. |
| 11–12| Measure + optimise  | 8-week analytics review; A/B test 2 hero variations + 2 form variations; tune `BAND_BY_TIER` against actual quote → close data; revisit this document and update for Q2. |

---

## 20. Top priorities

If only five things get done in the next 14 days, do these in this order:

1. **Fix the title double-suffix bug** (`SEO-T-3`). 10 minutes of work; every SERP impression improves immediately.
2. **Install Vercel Web Analytics + Plausible + wire the 7 events from `T-3`.** Without measurement, every subsequent decision is guesswork.
3. **Ship `/og-default.jpg` + per-area `opengraph-image.tsx`.** Stops social shares from looking broken.
4. **Add a photo gallery + 3 real testimonials.** Single biggest conversion lever in the construction category.
5. **Reduce form friction (phone optional + clearer success state) and add unique "recent work in {area}" blocks on the top 10 traffic areas.** Lifts form completion ~20% and de-risks thin-content classification on the rest of the 59.

